LLab: Hard Drive Troubleshooting

Objective

The computer can not boot into the Windows OS. I have to diagnose and fix the problem so the computer boots into Windows every time. 

Environment

Tools Used

None

Operating System

Windows 11 Pro

Skills Practiced

Troubleshooting
System configuration

Actions Performed

Turned on the computer, the screen displayed No bootable devices found. 
Rebooted into BIOS and examined Boot Sequence settings. The internal HDD setting was disabled and out of order.
Reconfigured and configured Boot Sequence settings
Restarted the computer and tested the results
Documented findings

Commands Used

None

Verification

Successfully restarted the computer twice, each time booting into Windows OS. 

Issues Encountered

None

Resolution

Enabled the Internal HDD Setting in the boot sequence setting in the BIOS and prioritized the order of the boot sequence.

Key Takeaways

Replicating user issues can provide additional context for what the user is reporting.
Verification is an important troubleshooting step.

